================================================================================================================
SUMMARY
================================================================================================================
  The forest under FK1's local trigger (question A, the forest):
  - Controls: L357's V1 reproduced exactly (C1).  The gas proxy, fed L366's own history and the measured bias of its
    triggered mass, reproduces the PM's measured flux deviation (x1.13 at z = 2); the total-matter proxy would fail that
    same passing construction (T^2(k=5) = 0.25) -- so it is not a forest proxy for kicked carriers (C2).
  - FK1's trigger converts every halo above M_min whole for z <= 3 (nominal cell), F_b = 0.17 by z = 3,
    earlier than the PM's mesh trigger (H1).
  - Calibrated gas proxy at z = 2: nominal 0.027, FDM floor 0.027, upper bracket 0.015
    against DE11's 0.10 (H2): the nominal cell is AT the line, not safely inside it.
  - Window (W): forest zeta >= 1.00 (plain) / 1.00 (sqrt sigma); the flagship's worst-case bound is the
    own-density cap, zeta <= 2.70 (canonical) / 3.22 (alt) for the 1e12 host (the trigger's reach
    alone would allow 12.7); the resolved bound is XR12_stream_shells W2.
  - The smooth web's cone enhancement (an estimate) gives nominal 0.036 / upper 0.015
    (K; its pre-declared 'both brackets over 10%' did not hold: the smooth web converts late, z <~ 2.5, when F_b(2) jumps to
    0.95 -- harmless to the z = 2-3 gas but a threat to everything after it, flagged for S8 / X-COP).

  checks: 3/6 pass; load-bearing failures: 2   [183s]
